r the function $y=f(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3$ shown above, what is the expression for the area $A$ as a definite integral?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-30273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We want to express the area $A$ between the function $f(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis, between $x=-1$ and $x=1.$\n\nThis can be expressed as the definite integral of $f(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3$ between the lower limit $x=-1$ and the upper limit $x=1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-30273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d6317e4b24f953776249e6db2b9d49942736e1c4f5f9a98ef66656a5d14914f"} {"question" "q-30273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-30273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "A={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "A={\\int }_{-3}^{3}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x"] ["math" "A={\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-30273" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ the lower bound is $a=0,$ and the upper bound is $b=1.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{n}=\\frac{1}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(0+i\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d6317e4b24f953776249e6db2b9d49942736e1c4f5f9a98ef66656a5d14914f"} {"question" "q-113881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1+\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2+\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-73159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{4}2{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-73159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{l}=a+lΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}2{x}^{-4}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=2{x}^{-4},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-(1)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}2{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+l\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{3l}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[2{(1+\\frac{3l}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-73159" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d6317e4b24f953776249e6db2b9d49942736e1c4f5f9a98ef66656a5d14914f"} {"question" "q-73159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-73159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[16{(\\frac{7l}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{7}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[2{(1+\\frac{3l}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[2{(4+\\frac{l}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[\\frac{1}{16}{(\\frac{3l}{n})}^{-3}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"] ["math" "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{4l}{n})}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-73159" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[2{(1+\\frac{3l}{n})}^{-4}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-346179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express ${\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x$ as the limit of a left Riemann sum.\n\n*Hint: Write down the missing expression in terms of $i$ and $n.$*\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[(($\n{{field-1}}\n$)^{3}+2($\n{{field-2}}\n$)+1)\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-346179" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{3}+2x+1,$ the lower bound is $a=0,$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-0}{n}=\\frac{2}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(0+i\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(\\frac{2i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[({(\\,\\frac{2i}{n}\\,)}^{3}+2(\\,\\frac{2i}{n}\\,)+1)\\,\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"que