7d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A definite integral can be defined as the limit of a left Riemann sum as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})\\cdot Δx\n$$\n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx.$\n\nNotice that we're given that the lower limit $a=0.$ \n\nComparing the given summation with the general expression above, we see that $Δx=\\frac{2}{n}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{n}=\\frac{b-0}{n}\\,⟹\\,b=2.\n$$\n\nConsequently,  ${x}_{k}=\\frac{2k}{n}$ and $f({x}_{k})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{x}_{k}.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2k}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $b=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113917" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d6317e4b24f953776249e6db2b9d49942736e1c4f5f9a98ef66656a5d14914f"} {"question" "q-113917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14080406/state.json" "file_sha256" "71e4e23ce6ffc25942b10962382cc682087d08e505f08efd8deda2bb5d09496f"} {"question" "q-113917" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$f(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and $b=2$"] ["text" "$f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}